  "instruction": "You are given template `/home/user/Desktop/blade_mode.fst`. Complete blade modal analysis from the command line: 1. Modify the main file `/home/user/Desktop/blade_mode.fst`: - Disable wind field, aerodynamics, and control (keep only structural DOFs) - Enable linearization: `Linearize=True`, `NLinTimes=1` 2. Modify ElastoDyn to enable blade DOFs (`FlapDOF1/2`, `EdgeDOF1`), and disable tower and drivetrain DOFs. 3. Run: `cd outputs && openfast blade_mode` 4. Write a post-processing script to parse the `.lin` file: - Extract eigenvalues and compute first blade flapwise and first edgewise frequencies (Hz) - NREL 5MW references: flapwise ~0.65 Hz, edgewise ~0.60 Hz 5. Save to `/home/user/Desktop/summary.txt` in this format: `flap1_hz, edge1_hz` 6. Do not use GUI tools. [Init Package Note] - Additional initialization dependencies are pre-uploaded under `/home/user/Desktop` with relative structure preserved. - Continue following the original task workflow: generate/modify required files and compute outputs yourself. - Only initialization inputs are included; no answer/result artifacts are preloaded.",
